# Go style for {{.Config.Project.Name}}

Overrides, which take precedence:

- Do not add explanatory inline or trailing comments in Go code.
- Exported application symbols require documentation comments.
- A declaration's documentation comment has at most two physical lines, each at most 150 Unicode characters including `//`.

Then follow, in order:
[Go Code Review Comments](https://go.dev/wiki/CodeReviewComments),
[Go in production: formatting and style](https://peter.bourgon.org/go-in-production/#formatting-and-style), and
[Uber Go Style Guide](https://github.com/uber-go/guide/blob/master/style.md) where compatible.
The full policy is in `.rubric/style.md`.
{{if .Lint}}
Check mechanically with `sh .rubric/check.sh lint`, which runs golangci-lint and the comment analyzer in `.rubric/style`.
{{else}}
Linting is not enabled for this project; review these rules by reading the code and format it with `gofmt`.
{{end -}}
